    "problem_statement": "## Chat Message Window Compressor\n\nA messaging platform wants to analyze chat logs for moderation. Each log is a string of lowercase English letters, where each character represents a message category code. The platform wants to find the **length of the longest substring that contains at most `k` distinct category codes**.\n\nGiven a string `log` and an integer `k`, return the length of the longest contiguous substring of `log` that contains at most `k` distinct characters.\n\nIf `k` is 0 or the string is empty, return 0.\n\n### Function Signature\n```python\ndef longest_window_k_distinct(log: str, k: int) -> int:\n```\n\n### Input Format\n- A string `log` of lowercase English letters.\n- An integer `k`.\n\n### Output Format\n- A single integer: the length of the longest substring with at most `k` distinct characters.",
