        "approach": "Use a variable sliding window. Expand the right pointer to include new characters. Use a frequency map to track the count of each character in the current window. When the number of distinct characters (keys with count > 0) in the map exceeds k, shrink the window from the left: decrement the frequency of the leftmost character, and if it drops to zero, remove it from the map (reducing distinct count by 1). At each step, update the maximum window size. Both pointers move at most n steps total, giving O(n) time.",
        "code": "def longest_window_k_distinct(log: str, k: int) -> int:\n    if k == 0 or not log:\n        return 0\n\n    freq = {}    # character -> count in current window\n    left = 0\n    max_len = 0\n\n    for right in range(len(log)):\n        char = log[right]\n        freq[char] = freq.get(char, 0) + 1   # expand window to the right\n\n        # Shrink from the left while we have more than k distinct chars\n        while len(freq) > k:\n            left_char = log[left]\n            freq[left_char] -= 1\n            if freq[left_char] == 0:\n                del freq[left_char]           # remove character entirely\n            left += 1\n\n        max_len = max(max_len, right - left + 1)\n\n    return max_len",
